# The basis: the recommended environment for running pero-ocr on its own (Python 3.8, 3.9 or 3.10), and the exact versions
# the tests, the frozen data and the Docker image use. Tested in production on Python 3.10, with variants on 3.8 and 3.9
# (issue #94, "Stable dependency basis"). pyproject.toml loosens it for other projects that depend on pero-ocr; this file
# pins one point inside its ranges.
#
# Regenerate requirements/lock.txt after changing this file:
#   uv pip compile requirements/lock.in -o requirements/lock.txt --python-version 3.8 \
#       --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu118 --index-strategy unsafe-best-match \
#       --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --emit-index-url
